) emerged as the first political party in the Netherlands dedicated solely to animal rights and environmental issues. Based in Amsterdam, this institution has gained traction in a country known for its progressive stance on social issues, marking a significant shift in political discourse towards ecological and ethical considerations in governance. It was established by Marianne Thieme, a prominent animal rights advocate, whose leadership helped frame the party's platform around welfare for animals and sustainable environmental policies.

